%% One Slack message, end to end, with relaygate on (charts/slack-relay + charts/relaygate).
%% Source of truth for slack-relay-flow.svg / .png. Render with
%% @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli 11.4.2: mmdc -i slack-relay-flow.mmd -o slack-relay-flow.svg -b white
%% and the same with -o slack-relay-flow.png -s 2.
%% Steps 3-5 and 9-10 go through relaygate once its proxy (build 2) ships; until then
%% and without relaygate, the router and host talk to Relaycast directly.
%%{init: {"theme": "base", "themeVariables": {"fontSize": "15px", "lineColor": "#475569", "primaryTextColor": "#0f172a"}, "sequence": {"mirrorActors": false, "wrap": true, "width": 190}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant P as Person in Slack
  participant R as Router (ledger)
  participant G as relaygate (optional)
  participant C as Relaycast
  participant H as Agent host
  participant A as Thread's agent (Claude Code)

  P->>R: @app question (Socket Mode event)
  R->>R: record in the ledger (dedupe), look up the thread's agent<br/>new thread → new agent (or a pinned one)
  R->>G: post to the thread's relay thread (rg_ token)
  G->>G: mode check (group 22 → stream 660)
  G->>C: forward
  C->>H: event for the thread's agent
  H->>A: wake: resume its session, run one turn
  A-->>H: answer
  H->>G: reply in the relay thread as the agent
  G->>C: forward
  C->>R: thread reply from the owning agent
  R->>G: /v1/check: may this text go to slack:T/C/thread?
  G->>G: mode check, then classifier (rules + model)
  alt allow
    G-->>R: allow
    R->>P: post the answer in the Slack thread
  else deny
    G-->>R: 403 relaygate_classified
    R->>R: record outbound.withheld
    R->>P: "That answer was withheld by policy."
  end
  Note over G,C: proxy steps (3-5, 9-10): relaygate build 2, planned. Today agents reach Relaycast directly.
  Note over H,A: between messages the agent is idle, with no process running
